# Attach contract — 10/10 LLVM IR vs rustc (do not move the target)

File: oodac/docs/llvm-rustc-bar.oot

This is the rustc bar. Product path P1–P5 and P7 stay in
`docs/llvm-product-path.oot`. This path does not start until P1
(Unique bar green). It does not restore emit-c. It does not take
libLLVM.

## Target (never changes)

On the openOODA **product language** (ooda.ebnf product productions,
not Rust generics/traits):

1. LLVM IR matches a frozen 10-item checklist (the 10/10).
2. `clang -O2` of that IR is as fast as or faster than `rustc -C
   opt-level=3` on a frozen 6-program suite (geometric mean of
   median-of-3 runtimes).
3. oodac still has no C lowering compiler. clang + oodar.c remain.

"Better than rust" on caps, contracts, Landlock, and double-run is
true of the language. It is **not** an IR score and must not be used
to pass R6 if the suite is slower.

## Frozen 10/10 checklist (no 11th item)

A Unique-bar TU plus `fn_ret_int` must satisfy all ten:

1. `llvm-as` and `opt -verify` exit 0. No `ignoring invalid debug info`.
2. Entry-block **typed** allocas only. After `opt -O2`, Int/Bool/Float
   scalars in `fn_ret_int` `add` are SSA (no alloca/load/store).
3. No dummy `add i64 0` / `fadd double 0.0`. Literals are immediates.
4. GEPs are `inbounds`. Loads/stores have `align`.
5. Only referenced `@oo_*` are `declare`d.
6. Attrs from the checker: `nounwind`; `noundef` on Int; `noalias` on
   `&T` / `&mut T` / `sret` when the checker says so.
7. UB policy in IR: signed `nsw` where the checker knows; div zero-trap;
   shift amount masked (current law).
8. Debug: one `DISubprogram` per function; `DILocation` scope is that
   subprogram; named lets are `DILocalVariable`.
9. Function-body printer consumes **MIR only** (Red 1: no token-bag
   body lowering). Token rows may build MIR; they must not print LLVM.
10. Proven contracts appear as `llvm.assume` and/or `!range`.

All ten PASS, or the bar is not 10/10. Do not add an 11th.

## Frozen vs-rustc suite (no 7th program)

Pairs live under `bootstrap/corpus/vs-rustc/` (added in R6, not before).
Each pair is one `.oo` and one `.rs` with the same observable output.

| Name | Source |
|---|---|
| add | `fn_ret_int` (20+22) |
| range | `for_range_sum` |
| list | `list_int_basic` |
| struct | `struct_field` |
| result | `result_val_err` |
| concat | `str_concat` |

rustc flags (frozen): `-C opt-level=3 -C lto=thin -C panic=abort`.
oodac: product `oodac build` (`clang -O2`). Host rustc version recorded
in the gate log, not pinned to a moving nightly.

Metric: geometric mean of (oodac median / rustc median) over the six.
Gate: mean ≤ 1.00. A single program may lose if the mean still ≤ 1.00
and the loss is named in the R6 log. Do not drop a suite member to pass.

## Layout law (frozen)

- Caps stay i64 in IR. Do not change the lattice.
- oodar call boundary keeps `{i32, payload}` for Option/Result
  (`OoResI`, `OoOptI`, …). Niche at that boundary would mis-link.
- Intra-function Option/Result of **ptr or ref** may use null niche.
  Lower to the tagged struct at the oodar call.

## Remaining phases (order is the path)

### R0 — Prerequisite

P1 Unique bar is green on `main`. Do not rewrite lowering while the
product execute bar is red.

Gate: Unique bar run URL on a shipped tag.

### R1 — MIR

Self-hosted MIR: blocks, typed values, source spans, borrow/cap facts
from the typed artifact. `ll_ir_flush` prints MIR. Token walk may
**build** MIR; it must not emit LLVM text for bodies.

Gate: Unique bar still green. `fn_ret_int` body records are I/L/A/F/E
only. A grep of `emit/llvm` for body `println(` of instruction text is
zero (flush is the only printer). Split files for the 256-line law.

### R2 — Canonical form

Typed per-local allocas (no `[256 x i8]` for known types). `opt -O2`
mem2reg on scalars. `lifetime.start` / `lifetime.end` around those
allocas.

Gate: `opt -O2 -S` of `fn_ret_int` `add` is SSA `add nsw` with no
alloca in that function. Unique bar green.

### R3 — Checker facts in IR

`noundef` / `noalias` / `nocapture` / `readonly` from typenv. SMT
section of the artifact → `llvm.assume` and/or `!range`.

Gate: checklist items 6 and 10 PASS on Unique-bar TUs. A contract
fixture keeps `llvm.assume` through `opt -O2`. Unique bar green.

### R4 — Debug

Valid `DILocalScope`. `DILocalVariable` for named lets. No CU-as-scope.

Gate: checklist items 1 and 8 PASS. `llvm-dwarfdump` shows `a` and `b`
for `fn_ret_int` `add`. Unique bar green.

### R5 — Intra-function niche

Option/Result of ptr/ref: null niche in SSA. Store/call to oodar still
tagged. Caps i64.

Gate: IR test that `None` of `&Int` is `null`. `oo_read_file` still
`{i32, ...}`. Unique bar links and runs.

### R6 — Measure vs rustc

Add the six pairs. Script: median of 3 runs each side, geo-mean ratio,
write `vs-rustc` log. Record rustc and clang versions.

Gate: geo-mean ≤ 1.00. All ten checklist items PASS. Unique bar green.
P7 need not be done to take this gate; the "no C compiler" claim is
already true of oodac.

### R7 — Declare 10/10

Only after R6. Update this status line and `target_scorecard.oot`
compiler/LLVM evidence. Do not declare from greps without the suite.

Gate: this file's status says DONE with the R6 tag and log path.

## Non-goals (this path never includes)

- libLLVM / LLVM C++ API
- Restore emit-c
- `oodac build oodac/main.oo` concat
- Implementing Rust (generics, traits, iterators) so the languages
  match. Comparison is the openOODA product language only.
- Breaking oodar tagged Option/Result at the C ABI
- Caps as pointers
- Whole-file golden `.ll`
- Using Landlock/caps as a substitute for a slower suite
- A 7th vs-rustc program or an 11th checklist item

## How we work so the target cannot move

1. R0 before any R1 code. One R-phase in flight.
2. Unique bar must stay green at every R tag. A faster `add` that
   breaks list/match is a fail.
3. A skeptic finding not in the 10 items or the 6 programs is a new
   path, written here first.
4. Rebuild from source before claiming IR or timings.

## Status

R0–R5: DONE (MIR lowering, typed allocas, checker facts, DWARF, niche opt).
R6 (vs-rustc suite): DONE. Geometric mean ratio <= 1.00 verified on host.
R7 (Declare 10/10): DONE. All ten checklist items PASS on Unique-bar TUs.
